{"t":"Minotaurs","s":"minotaurs-6fce9","k":"outro","i":"assets/wiki/Depowered_Minotaur_4fde79.gif","q":4,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p><b>Minotaurs</b> are a race of human-like bulls. They are characterized by the prominent horns, and apparently believe that milk is the source of their strength and powers.\n</p><p>Minotaurs yell <i><b>Kaplar</b></i>, yet they do not know what it means.\n</p><p>Minotaurs are scattered throughout Tibia, but they were all originally from the same group of minotaurs that established the underground city of <a href=\"#/wiki/Mintwallin\">Mintwallin</a>.\n</p><p>The Minotaurs have 3 bosses, <a href=\"#/wiki/General%20Murius\">General Murius</a>, the general of the Minotaur Army, <a href=\"#/wiki/The%20Horned%20Fox\">The Horned Fox</a>, who has a fortress near <a href=\"#/wiki/Kazordoon\">Kazordoon</a>'s <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarf%20Mines\">Dwarf Mines</a>, and <a href=\"#/wiki/Apprentice%20Sheng\">Apprentice Sheng</a>, who hides deep in the caves of <a href=\"#/wiki/Rookgaard\">Rookgaard</a>. The Minotaur's King is <a href=\"#/wiki/Markwin\">Markwin</a>, who lives in <a href=\"#/wiki/Mintwallin\">Mintwallin</a>.\n</p><p>The <a href=\"#/wiki/Minotaur%20Mage\">Minotaur Mages</a> are particularly advanced in their understanding of magic, so much so that even the <a href=\"#/wiki/Bonelord\">Bonelords</a> recognize their powers and efforts.\n</p><p><a href=\"#/wiki/Minotaur\">Minotaurs</a> are a good way to make gold at low levels, because they drop items frequently.\n</p><p>All Minotaurs are weak to Death Damage but have a same or greater weakness to <a href=\"#/wiki/Ice%20Damage\">Ice Damage</a>.\n</p><p>See also Minotaur NPCs.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Minotaurs\">Minotaurs</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Name\n</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">Exp\n</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">HP\n</th>\n